{"pageid": 903, "title": "Emerald Mask", "revid": 2168, "categories": ["Emerald Masks", "Lore", "Masks", "Monster hunters", "Order of St. George"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/8/85/Emerald_Mask.png/revision/latest?cb=20241130215823\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"The Emerald Mask of the North American Houses.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/8/85/Emerald_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241130215823\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"98\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Emerald Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"Emerald_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Emerald_Mask.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">The Emerald Mask of the North American Houses.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<p><b>Emerald Masks</b> are a branch of <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a> who don the color green. They are the highest-ranking of all other masks except for the <a href=\"/wiki/House_Dragons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"House Dragons\">House Dragons</a> and possibly <a href=\"/wiki/Violet_Masks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Violet Masks\">Violet Masks</a>, though that is currently unclear, due to the fact they have been trained to hunt and kill <span class=\"new\" title=\"Dragons (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRHJhZ29ucz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Dragons</span>, the most vicious and deadly of all <a href=\"/wiki/Monsters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Monsters\">Monsters</a>. With the slow decline of Dragons appearing in the modern world, Emerald Masks are very rare, and usually found in countries with deep dragon folklore.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>Emerald Masks are the highest class of monster hunter within the Order of St. George, and require the most training. They are the dragon hunters, following in the steps of the Founder of the Order, St. George. There are two ways to earn an Emerald Mask: one requires being chosen to train as a Silver Mask, rising to the status of Master at that rank, and then undergoing years of training at the Great House of St. George; the other requires finding and killing a dragon in the wild. Dragons are born from mankind's most primal and powerful emotions, and most form in societies with a deep cultural belief in dragons. There are few dragons left in the world today, and even fewer Emerald Masks.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Slaughter_1\" title=\"Book of Slaughter 1\">The Book of Slaughter</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The Emerald Masks are the Dragon-Hunters of each house. Becoming an Emerald Mask is a difficult task, and requires extreme training and discipline.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOS&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOS-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> As Dragons are the most dangerous of all Monsters, those who hunt Dragons have to be just as dangerous.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> As the founder of the Order, St. George himself, began the organization after slaying a dragon, this branch is extremely well-regarded and respected among all other members.\n</p><p>There are two ways to earn an Emerald Mask. The first is to find and kill a dragon in the wild; all dragon-killers will automatically be regarded as Emeralds. However, with the lack of dragons, most of the remaining Emerald Masks gain their color by first training as a <a href=\"/wiki/Silver_Masks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Silver Masks\">Silver Mask</a>. They then have to become a Master at that rank, and then go to <span class=\"new\" title=\"The Great House of St. George (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGhlX0dyZWF0X0hvdXNlX29mX1N0Ll9HZW9yZ2U/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">the Great House</span> in order to train in secret for multiple years.\n</p><p>Many houses no longer have Emerald Masks, simply due to a lack of need for them.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOS&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOS-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"0fbd8161c38d636aa1e8c87c1fe4fa2d\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:103px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Emerald_Mask-png\" style=\"position: relative; height:101px; width:185px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Emerald_Mask.png\" title=\"Emerald Mask.png (339 KB)\" style=\"height:101px; width:185px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/8/85/Emerald_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/185?cb=20241130215823\" title=\"Emerald Mask.png (339 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"\" height=\"101\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Emerald Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"Emerald_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\"></noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" title=\"Emerald Mask.png (339 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" alt=\"\" height=\"101\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Emerald Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"Emerald_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/8/85/Emerald_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/185?cb=20241130215823\" /></a></div></div></div></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span></h2>\n<small><div style=\"width:auto; max-height:190px; overflow:auto; padding-left:0.5em; padding-right:0.5em; border-top-left-radius:0.5em; border-bottom-left-radius:0.5em\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-BOS-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOS_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOS_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">Tynion, James IV</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Slaughter_1\" title=\"Book of Slaughter 1\">Book of Slaughter</a>,</i> vol. #1, <a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Slaughter_1\" title=\"Book of Slaughter 1\">issue no.1</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>, 2022.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-BOB-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOB_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">Tynion, James IV</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">Book of Butcher</a>,</i> vol. #1, <a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">issue no.1</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>, 2023.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div></small></div>", "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T22:43:30+00:00"}